FUNDAMENTALS (Csikszentmihalyi Flow Model)

Variables:
  C  = perceived challenge of the task
  S  = perceived skill / competence
  Δ  = C − S   (mismatch)

Core rule:
  Flow occurs when C ≈ S and both are high.

State map (by Δ and magnitude):

  High C, Low  S  →  ANXIETY   (fear of failure, overwhelm)
  High C, Mid  S  →  AROUSAL / WORRY
  High C, High S  →  FLOW      (absorption, time distortion)
  Mid  C, High S  →  CONTROL
  Low  C, High S  →  BOREDOM   (loss of interest)
  Low  C, Mid  S  →  RELAXATION
  Low  C, Low  S  →  APATHY
  Mid  C, Low  S  →  WORRY / DOUBT

Practical levers:
  Raise C when bored  → add difficulty, constraints, stakes
  Raise S when anxious → practice, decompose, get feedback
  Keep both rising together to stay inside the flow channel
